Dear Franz,

I have seen something which might be related, under DU 3.2C. If the
DISPLAY variable is set to "local:0.0" then whenever emacs version 19 is
started both the emacs process and the Xdec process chew up CPU time.
The solution was to change the DISPLAY variable to ":0.0" (either by
hand, or by editing /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xservers .

Bob
