>>DOS 6.22 (don't ask!).  The PC has a 3com network adapter.  What I would
>>like to do is to have the PC be able to access the filesystem on the
>>Alphastation (including the filesystem on the MO drive, if mounted). 
>>When I say, "access", I don't mean telnet or ftp, but I mean really
>>access as if the unix filesystem were mounted on the PC.  The reason I
>>want to do this is so that I can backup the PC's files onto the MO
>>drive.  Any help , would be much appreciated.
>>
>>Thanks,
>>
>>Dr. Vincent Ferrera
>>Columbia University
>>vpf3@columbia.edu

There are other ways than NFS.  You could ftp the files over and move
them onto the MO drive via an rsh command. 

There is a version of NFS called XFS out and about on the web.  I have
used this to access an SGI Indigo system from some DOS boxes.  Worked
pretty slick.  I have also used PC-NFS, at a considerably higher cost.


The unix system mounts as drives and DOS commands work to copy files
back and forth.  In order to maintain DOS filenames when backing up
files from the DOS box to the SGI I pkzip them over.

Lots of fun stuff you can do between DOS and Unix.

Good luck,

Dale Kittlesen






