On different versions of SysV, the posix shell is put in different
locations.  We're considering installing a softlink on every system
here, so that shell scripts can refer to the posix shell and always
find it in the same place (no matter what vendor's system is used).

On HP-UX 10.x, the posix shell is /usr/bin/sh and with a softlink to
/usr/bin/posix/sh.

On Solaris 2.x, the posix shell is found at /usr/bin/ksh with a
softlink to /usr/xpg4/bin/sh.

On Motorola AIX 4.1, the posix shell is only found at /usr/bin/ksh.

What is the concensus on where a posixshell softlink should reside?  One
of the alternatives I've tossed around is /opt/posix/sh as a pointer to
