You've seen the post on one solution, SAMBA. That gives you SMB drive
(simulation) on UNIX host and you can mount it on PC Windows machine.
Not bad, as I've heard. Now, here's another, I've tried it myself.

You can enable PC-NFS daemon (and that's what you wanted, I think) and
install NFS client on your PC. The only such client I know of is the one
in Lan WorkPlace Pro, but there could be others. Oh, and when you do
that, you must have an account on Alpha, because PC must authenticate
itself. Authentication is done via that account. LWP Pro NFS will ask
for username and password.

Cheers,
