Folks:

I have a few questions about DEC's new dtmail mail program delivered with the
Common Desktop Environment that I hope somebody out there knows the answer to.
I've been looking forward to support from DEC for MIME-based mail, but it looks
like they've made it very difficult to move to this new mailer.

1.  Is dtmail an mh-based mail program?  I was surprised to see that it didn't
seem to recognize my already existing folders from dxmail.  Also, I use several
mh-based mailers, including some which are usable from VT100 terminals (emacs,
Pine), so conversion to a new format is not an option for me.  Another reason
that conversion is not an option is that at least temporarily some of our
computers will be running OSF v4 and will not have the CDE available to them,
but they all share the same disks.

2.  Is there a way to specify what editor to use within dtmail?  In dxmail,
there's a nice Editor button which allows you to switch to the editor of your
choice.  For me, that's emacs.

Thank you,

William Thompson



